  "id": "secondary-cause",
  "term": "secondary cause",
  "definition": "In this historical philosophical use, a secondary cause is a subordinate agency placed between God as the primary efficient source and the particular details of the world. It refers to nature understood not as independent, but as an intermediate principle through which events are brought about.",
